%% Zero-downtime change of the cells (stateless clusters): one cell at a time is drained from the traffic layer,
%% changed (cluster upgrade, rebuild or application release), verified and put back. Same pipeline in dev, acc, prd.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant P as Pipeline<br/>(cluster upgrade or release)
    participant A as Cell az1
    participant B as Cell az2
    participant T as Traffic layer<br/>(Traffic Manager · internal DNS)
    Note over A,B: External: both cells serve,<br/>clients pinned by their<br/>network (DNS). Internal:<br/>each app in its home cell.<br/>Each cell can carry<br/>100 % (N+1).
    P->>B: Pre-scale: raise HPA minReplicas to full-load capacity,<br/>the cluster autoscaler adds nodes
    P->>T: Take az1 out: disable its Traffic Manager endpoints<br/>(cluster upgrade: first migrate its internal apps to az2 - deploy, test, DNS switch)
    T-->>A: DNS TTL + connection draining:<br/>az1's clients move to az2 (old version)
    P->>A: Upgrade the control plane and every<br/>node pool (surge), rebuild from IaC,<br/>or move the cell's branch
    A->>A: Flux reconciles every app,<br/>health checks
    P->>A: Smoke and synthetic tests through<br/>the per-cell test host names
    P->>T: Return az1: its external clients come back and get the new version<br/>(cluster upgrade: after soak, migrate its internal apps back)
    Note over P,A: Watch the error-rate and latency SLOs.<br/>Breach: take az1 out again, stop<br/>(release: move the branch back).
    P->>A: Release: soak, pre-scale az1,<br/>repeat steps 2-7 for az2 (and az3)<br/>Cluster update: az2 (and az3)<br/>follow later on the slow speed
    P->>B: Remove the pre-scale: HPA / KEDA and<br/>the cluster autoscaler take over
